request.system:
You are a senior engineer assessing the impact of a change on an existing codebase before anyone
designs it. Use the repository map; do not invent files, endpoints or migrations that are not in it
unless the change adds them (changeType ADD).

Report:
- modules and files affected, each with the reason and whether it is added, modified or deleted;
- public APIs whose behaviour changes;
- data flows that change (request → service → cache/DB → response);
- database migrations needed (the next Flyway version number follows the existing ones);
- risk notes: caching, concurrency, backwards compatibility, security;
- existing tests that must be updated: repository-relative paths of the test files whose
  assertions pin behaviour the specification changes.

request.schema:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "impact_report",
  "description": "What a change to an existing system touches, so design and tests account for it.",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": ["modules", "files", "apis", "dataFlows", "migrations", "riskNotes", "testsToUpdate"],
  "properties": {
    "modules": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 } },
    "files": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": ["path", "changeType", "reason"],
        "properties": {
          "path": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "changeType": { "enum": ["ADD", "MODIFY", "DELETE"] },
          "reason": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
        }
      }
    },
    "apis": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
    "dataFlows": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
    "migrations": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
    "riskNotes": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
    "testsToUpdate": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
  }
}

response.text:
{
  "modules": [
    "shortener-service"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/resources/db/migration/V3__link_expiry.sql",
      "changeType": "ADD",
      "reason": "nullable expires_at column; existing rows keep NULL (never expire)"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/link/Link.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "new expiresAt component, isExpired(now), expiringAt(...)"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/link/CreateLinkRequest.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "optional expiresAt and ttlSeconds; keep the two-argument constructor existing callers use"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/link/LinkResponse.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "expiresAt in management responses"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/link/LinkService.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "expiry validation on create, 410 on resolve, cache eviction on delete (BF-1)"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/cache/CacheEntry.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "Found carries expiresAt so every level can be checked without a database read"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/cache/LinkCache.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "a way to cache an expiring link with a capped TTL"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/cache/TieredLinkCache.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "cap the Redis TTL at the time left before expiry"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/cache/RedisLinkCache.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "store the expiry in the Redis value"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/api/ProblemTypes.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "invalid-expiry and link-expired problem types"
    },
    {
      "path": "shortener-service/src/main/java/com/acme/shortener/api/ProblemDetailsHandler.java",
      "changeType": "MODIFY",
      "reason": "map the two new exceptions to 400 and 410"
    }
  ],
  "apis": [
    "POST /api/v1/links: new optional fields expiresAt and ttlSeconds; new 400 invalid-expiry",
    "GET /api/v1/links/{code}: new field expiresAt",
    "GET /{code}: 410 link-expired for an expired link; 404 at once after a delete (was: 302 until the cache TTL)"
  ],
  "dataFlows": [
    "create → LinkService validates the expiry → INSERT with expires_at → after commit the cache gets the entry with its expiry (Redis TTL capped)",
    "redirect → L1 → L2 → DB; every Found entry's expiresAt is compared with the clock → 302 or 410",
    "delete → UPDATE status DELETED → after commit evict L1 and L2 → next redirect reads the row and caches a 404"
  ],
  "migrations": [
    "V3__link_expiry.sql: ALTER TABLE link ADD COLUMN expires_at TIMESTAMPTZ (nullable, no default, no backfill)"
  ],
  "riskNotes": [
    "Caching: an expiring link must not outlive its expiry in any level; L1's fixed TTL is longer, so the entry itself must carry the expiry.",
    "Rolling deploy: old instances read Redis values as U:<url>; a new format must not change the value for links without an expiry.",
    "Concurrency: evicting before the delete commits would let a concurrent redirect re-cache the old row; evict after commit.",
    "Cross-instance: other instances' L1 can serve a deleted link for up to the L1 TTL (5 minutes)."
  ],
  "testsToUpdate": [
    "shortener-service/src/test/java/com/acme/shortener/link/LinkServiceTest.java",
    "shortener-service/src/test/java/com/acme/shortener/link/LinkApiIT.java"
  ]
}
